  "body": "Not only me repeatedly in my Web programming history, but also many others users that work daily with canvases, including [Ricardo Cabello](https://twitter.com/mrdoob).\r\n\r\nThe `event.layerX` and `event.layerY` are [apparently not standard](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/UIEvent/layerX) but de-facto properties that has been around in every browser for years.\r\n\r\nThe behavior in Chrome is also aligned with the one in WebKit, and the usefulness of these coordinates is indisputable when it comes to draw on canvas that also uses exact same coordinates system.\r\n\r\nIs there any chance we can standardize these properties so that polyfills can be created for Edge / IE and all developers using canvas can create, store, and reproduce, shapes through these coordinates?\r\n\r\n`context.fillRect` as well as `context.strokeRect` as well as pretty much any other context2d method method uses by default a top left x,y coordinates system, which is the same provided by default in Chrome and WebKit with `event.layerX` and `event.layerY`.\r\n\r\nThanks for considering this improvement. The \"_drawing community_\" will surely appreciate.\r\n\r\nBest Regards.",
